[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119649,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma (B-ALL/LBL) with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em>-like features is a neoplasm of lymphoblasts of B-cell lineage characterized by a gene expression profile similar to that of B-ALL with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em>, in the absence of the <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em> translocation.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119650,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9814/3 B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em>-like features</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119651,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2A70.Y Other B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with recurrent genetic abnormalities</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119652,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> B-ALL, <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1&shy;&shy;</em>-like.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119653,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119654,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL and B-LBL represent the same disease. B-ALL always involves the bone marrow and usually also involves the peripheral blood. Extramedullary involvement is common and is by definition the primary site of involvement in B-LBL. For details, see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/385\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma</em> .</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119655,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>No unique features</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119656,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Like B-ALL/LBL with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em> fusion, B-ALL/LBL with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em>-like features is more frequent in childhood, representing 1&ndash;3% of B-ALL/LBL cases in this population {27265895}, and uncommon in adults {33895809}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119657,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119658,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Combined <em>ETV6</em> and <em>IKZF1</em> rearrangements or deletions appear common and specific to this entity, and they may underlie an alternative mechanism for <em>RUNX1</em> disruption in place of an <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em> fusion {19129520; 23823658; 27265895}. <em>ETV6</em> rearrangement partners in this category identified to date include <em>BCL2L14</em>, <em>BORCS5</em>, <em>CREBBP</em>, <em>MSH6</em>, <em>NID1</em>, and <em>PMEL</em> {27265895}. <em>ARPP21</em> deletion may be a secondary genetic event {28395118}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119659,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119660,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "\r\n<h5>Immunophenotype</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>Like B-ALL/LBL with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em> fusion, this type also demonstrates a CD27-positive, CD44-low-to-negative immunophenotype {28395118}.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119661,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119662,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The optimal clinical methods for the identification of this entity have not yet been established {33400146}. Like in B-ALL/LBL with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em> fusion, a high <em>RAG1</em> signature {33987955} and <em>IGF2BP3</em> {33805930} expression and a CD27-positive, CD44-low-to-negative immunophenotype {28395118} are suggestive but not fully specific {34535762}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119663,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> meets the diagnostic criteria for B-ALL/LBL (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/385\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma</em>); lack of <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em> translocation and other defined recurrent genetic abnormalities in B-ALL/LBL; gene expression profile similar to that of B-ALL/LBL with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em>.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> demonstration of a recognized <em>ETV6</em> fusion partner, with or without associated <em>IKZF1</em> alterations; demonstration of CD27-positive&nbsp;/ CD44-low-to-negative immunophenotype.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119664,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119665,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Because the number of patients identified as having B-ALL with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em>-like features is small, the outcome of patients with this subtype is still undefined. However, several relapses have been reported {34250504}. <em>IKZF1</em> deletions and other alterations may not confer an unfavourable prognosis in this context like they do in others {19129520}. Further studies are needed to determine the outcome of patients affected by B-ALL/LBL with <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em>-like features.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:28:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]